    narr:narration """Freya Free's profile runs from a single cutover-staffing exchange into its echo across later review threads. She opens with [simple willingness](narr:Expr_2HalyardOpsReadiness20260915_4) and [a request to see the plan](narr:Expr_2HalyardOpsReadiness20260915_5), then lays out [the supervisor arithmetic behind one region's rota](narr:Expr_2HalyardOpsReadiness20260915_11) and states [that the people simply don't exist](narr:Expr_2HalyardOpsReadiness20260915_12). She reframes the disagreement [from risk to arithmetic](narr:Expr_2HalyardOpsReadiness20260915_14), names [the one constraint that doesn't move](narr:Expr_2HalyardOpsReadiness20260915_16), and adds [a second, learning-based benefit of sequencing](narr:Expr_2HalyardOpsReadiness20260915_18). She qualifies herself — [she'd still favor sequencing with more staff, but less strongly, and would lead with staffing before the steering group](narr:Expr_2HalyardOpsReadiness20260915_22) — then sets [the dates-and-soak condition she needs](narr:Expr_2HalyardOpsReadiness20260915_28) and closes [content](narr:Expr_2HalyardOpsReadiness20260915_30). That same condition and close reappear verbatim in [a later review thread](narr:Expr_20260928_2_ReviewCommentTanyaTeamownerAfbbdc56Cd2A440EAd0E0_hb725287d6759_11) and [another](narr:Expr_20260928_1_ReviewCommentTinaTeammemberB4B484EaE94D4912B80BD_h8c260252a0a9_18), with [the same settled affirmation](narr:Expr_20260928_2_ReviewCommentTanyaTeamownerAfbbdc56Cd2A440EAd0E0_hb725287d6759_13) — the position carried forward, not re-argued.""" ;
    narr:reaction """What moved: the soak condition and the settled close are no longer one-off — they now appear verbatim in [two later review threads](narr:Expr_20260928_2_ReviewCommentTanyaTeamownerAfbbdc56Cd2A440EAd0E0_hb725287d6759_11), so the prior narration's 'condition carried forward' line is confirmed as a repeated, dated pattern rather than a single echo. The voice profile itself didn't shift: the same antithesis-first, plain-spoken register and calm-positive closes hold across both dates, so nothing in the old reading needed revising.""" ;
